      "info": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Two possible paths",
          "text": "A condition selects a path.\n\nIF handles the true case.\n\nELSE handles the false case.\n\nChallenge: What happens when available is false?\n\nThe ELSE branch prints Unavailable."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Include the boundary",
          "text": "Greater than excludes equality.\n\nGreater than or equal includes equality.\n\nMatch the condition to the rule.\n\nChallenge: Why does age > 12 not match the rule?\n\nIt rejects a pupil aged exactly 12, although the rule includes them."
        },
        {
          "id": "f3",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Three-way decisions",
          "text": "Some problems need more than two outcomes.\n\nCheck greater, less and equal cases.\n\nEach valid input should have an outcome.\n\nChallenge: What happens if the draw case is omitted?\n\nEqual values may get the wrong result or no intended output."
        },
        {
          "id": "f4",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Both conditions",
          "text": "AND is true when both conditions are true.\n\nUse it when both requirements must hold.\n\nCheck each requirement separately.\n\nChallenge: Can this member borrow the unavailable item?\n\nNo. Both membership and availability are required, and availability is false."
        },
        {
          "id": "f5",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Either condition",
          "text": "OR is true when at least one condition is true.\n\nIt is also true when both are true.\n\nDo not confuse OR with exactly one.\n\nChallenge: Does a person who meets both conditions qualify?\n\nYes. OR includes the case where both conditions are true."
        },
        {
          "id": "f6",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Nested decisions",
          "text": "A decision can sit inside another decision.\n\nThe outer path controls whether it is reached.\n\nIndentation helps show the structure.\n\nChallenge: If member is false, is the inner decision reached?\n\nNo. The outer IF body is skipped."
        }
      ],
